| id | obligation | enforced_today | today | required | case |
| M1 | Verifier | false | Accept | Reject | substitute W (Wg entry changed), same statement, same declared model, P3 -- the declared model is a string; the fresh W root is compared to nothing |
| M2 | Verifier | false | Accept | Reject | substitute W (Wd entry changed), same statement, same declared model, P3 -- every tensor of the layer is unbound, not only Wg |
| M3 | Verifier | true | Reject | Reject | copied candidate root: substitute proof relabelled with the honest proof's W root -- BINDING, not identity: the root is absorbed into the transcript, so a proof is bound to its own root; the honest root is itself fresh and approves nothing |
| M4 | Verifier | true | Reject | Reject | changed calibration table: verify under a statement with another table digest -- table digest is absorbed (layer.rs absorb_statement_v3) |
| M5 | Verifier | true | Reject | Reject | changed quantization shifts: verify under a statement with sh_g 7 -> 8 -- signed shifts are absorbed |
| M6 | Verifier | false | Accept | Reject | changed calibration EXPONENTS with identical shifts and table (rescaled export) -- exponents are not in StatementV3 and not in the proof; the approved manifest must pin them and the verifier must be handed them |
| M7 | Verifier | true | Reject | Reject | wrong approved identity: proof declared model A, verified as model B -- the header binds the DECLARATION (mode header in the transcript), not its truth |
| M8 | Verifier | true | Reject | Reject | wrong approved identity: proof declared model A, verified with no declared model -- same binding; `model=w-root` is a different header |
| M9 | Verifier | false | Accept | Reject | false declaration by the prover: substitute weights DECLARED as model A -- identical to M1 seen from the prover's side: the declaration is free |
| M10 | Verifier | true | Reject | Reject | tier swap: a P3 proof verified as P1 (public weights claimed) -- privacy tier is in the header; W row counts also differ |
| M11 | Verifier | false | Accept | Reject | layer swap (tensors): another layer's weights presented under this layer's statement -- nothing binds WHICH hidden tensors belong at position l |
| M12 | Verifier | true | Reject | Reject | layer swap (index): a proof made at l=1 verified under the l=0 statement -- the layer index is absorbed |
| M13 | Verifier | false | Accept | Reject | replay: one P3 proof presented twice for two different requests (same domain) -- the verifier receives no request identity; a request nonce / I-O commitment must enter the transcript (caller obligation today) |
| M14 | Verifier | true | Reject | Reject | replay under another transcript domain (caller-bound request context) -- enforced ONLY when the caller binds the request into the domain |
| M15 | Prover | false | Accept | Accept | reused randomness: the same seed twice on the same witness -- no verifier can detect reuse from one proof; a privacy failure, not a soundness one; prover-side obligation (OS entropy, `Some(seed)` only in tests) |
| M16 | Prover | false | Accept | Accept | reused randomness across DIFFERENT witnesses: same seed, substitute weights -- reuse is invisible to the single-proof verifier and leaks across proofs |
| M17 | Verifier | true | Reject | Reject | P1 positive comparison: substitute weights at the registered P1 boundary -- the registered PUBLIC root is compared before any transcript exists |
| M18 | Verifier | true | Accept | Accept | P1 positive comparison: the honest registered proof -- the baseline the P3 boundary must reach with a HIDING stable root |
